{"title":"WBJEE","category":"Engineering","bank":"wbjee","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","count":5,"questions":[{"id":118419,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"Which one of the following is a condensation polymer?","options":["PVC","Teflon","Dacron","Polystyrene"],"answer":2,"solution":"Dacron is a condensation polymer. It is also known as terylene. It is a polymer obtained by condensation reaction between ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at $420-460 \\mathrm{K}$ in the presence of zinc acetate-antimony trioxide catalyst.\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2018_che_a65.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_a65.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_a65.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2018","_marksId":"64a8144fe0ff5a5425a85a73"},{"id":118420,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"Silicon oil is obtained from the hydrolysis and polymerisation of","options":["trimetylchlorosilane and dimethyldichlorosilane","trimethylchlorosilane and methyldichlorosilane","methyltrichlorosilane and dimethyldichlorosilane","triethylchlorosilane and dimethyidichlorosilane"],"answer":0,"solution":"Silicon oil in a polymer of trimethylchloro silane and dimethyldichloro silane. These are useful as broad spectrum antifoaming agents. \r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2013_che_a53.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2013_che_a53.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2013_che_a53.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2013","_marksId":"64a813f9e0ff5a5425a85742"},{"id":118421,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"Which one of the following is an example of co-polymer?","options":["Buna-S","Teflon","PVC","Polypropylene"],"answer":0,"solution":"Hints : Buna -S is a co-polymer of butadiene and styrene\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252FtvD_KTjB-e45OrZWWi29dZjyx1emA0-uiPmtudBxlts.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2FtvD_KTjB-e45OrZWWi29dZjyx1emA0-uiPmtudBxlts.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2FtvD_KTjB-e45OrZWWi29dZjyx1emA0-uiPmtudBxlts.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2010","_marksId":"64a813c2e0ff5a5425a8553e"},{"id":118422,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"The catalyst used for olefin polymerization is","options":["Ziegler-Natta Catalyst","Wilkinson Catalyst","Raney nickel catalyst","Merrifield resin"],"answer":0,"solution":"$\\mathrm{TiCl}_3+\\left(\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_5\\right)_3 \\mathrm{Al}$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2009","_marksId":"64a813aee0ff5a5425a85480"},{"id":118423,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"The monomer used to produce orlon is","options":["$\\mathrm{CH}_2=\\mathrm{CHF}$","$\\mathrm{CH}_2=\\mathrm{CCl}_2$","$\\mathrm{CH}_2=\\mathrm{CHCl}$","$\\mathrm{CH}_2=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CN}$"],"answer":3,"solution":"Orlon or PAN\nMonomer $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_2=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CN}$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2009","_marksId":"64a813afe0ff5a5425a85483"}]}